# Citation metadata. GitHub renders it as "Cite this repository", and Zenodo
# reads it for the record of every GitHub release.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use lazy-tfm, please cite the paper below and the software, and the
  pretrained checkpoints you used: a fitted model's provenance_ records exactly
  which ones.
title: "LAZY: Lazy but Accurate z for Yinz"
abstract: >-
  Conditional probability distributions of a continuous target (a redshift,
  a metallicity, any z) from pretrained tabular foundation models, behind
  the scikit-learn API.
type: software
authors:
